WEBVTT

00:00:02.220 --> 00:00:03.690
That should do it.

00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:06.190
Okay, talk now.

00:00:06.750 --> 00:00:08.120
Start with your name!

00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:10.480
I want to hear about
 your swordsmanship, too!

00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:14.200
Do I just speak into this thing?

00:00:14.920 --> 00:00:16.590
I'm Kanzaki Sensui.

00:00:16.590 --> 00:00:17.910
As for the sword...

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:23.680
I was taken in by a foreign swordsman 
when I was just a baby.

00:00:25.030 --> 00:00:28.400
That man taught me everything he knew 
about western swordsmanship.

00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:33.570
When I turned fifteen, 
I was taken in by my current lord.

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:38.320
My lord had me practice 
at the Nen-ryuu dojo,

00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:41.570
so I can fight freely 
with one or two swords,

00:00:42.040 --> 00:00:44.230
even if they're barbarian swords.

00:00:45.270 --> 00:00:47.440
How many times do I swing 
my sword when practicing?

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:49.610
I don't count from the start.

00:00:50.650 --> 00:00:53.640
I start counting once it becomes difficult.

00:00:55.850 --> 00:01:00.590
After all, the "Nen" of Nen-ryuu comes 
from the school's main principle:

00:01:00.590 --> 00:01:03.250
victory through determined purpose.

00:01:07.450 --> 00:01:11.190
Sensui, you're looking stiff! 
Relax a bit more!

00:01:36.990 --> 00:01:39.570
<b>"Beyond the Maelstrom"</b>

00:01:42.650 --> 00:01:44.390
This is the residential area.

00:01:45.370 --> 00:01:48.240
We have about 50 normal people living here.

00:01:49.870 --> 00:01:52.780
Only 50 in a space this big?

00:01:52.780 --> 00:01:55.460
That's awfully few people.

00:01:56.240 --> 00:01:58.640
That's because the others 
have become Gibia.

00:02:00.460 --> 00:02:01.960
Here, dear.

00:02:01.960 --> 00:02:02.840
Thanks.

00:02:27.240 --> 00:02:29.900
Sensui, I have a favor to ask.

00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:32.110
Fight me.

00:02:35.560 --> 00:02:38.430
Hey now, I'd stop right there.

00:02:38.630 --> 00:02:42.340
This man's known 
as the Slayer of a Thousand.

00:02:42.340 --> 00:02:45.600
He's not the kind of guy you can beat, lady.

00:02:46.990 --> 00:02:50.100
Which of you is stronger, you or Sensui?

00:02:50.100 --> 00:02:51.080
Hmm?

00:02:52.300 --> 00:02:55.540
Well, the last time we fought...

00:02:55.540 --> 00:02:56.510
We were evenly matched.

00:02:56.510 --> 00:02:59.600
I could never best him with a sword,

00:02:59.600 --> 00:03:02.060
but battles aren't just 
about clashing swords.

00:03:02.530 --> 00:03:05.870
You're both just as strong as the other, then.

00:03:06.580 --> 00:03:09.680
We only have barely enough 
supplies for this camp,

00:03:10.640 --> 00:03:13.200
so I want to see for myself 
if you're truly strong...

00:03:13.740 --> 00:03:17.740
strong enough to protect us.

00:03:19.340 --> 00:03:21.700
If you really are a samurai,

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:24.990
then I want you to prove 
that you can fight Gibia, too.

00:03:25.390 --> 00:03:26.540
All right.

00:03:26.540 --> 00:03:28.540
You're not serious, are you?

00:03:29.570 --> 00:03:30.930
I have to do it.

00:03:31.470 --> 00:03:34.780
Kathleen-dono saved my life once already,

00:03:35.380 --> 00:03:38.010
so I can't ignore her requests.

00:03:38.780 --> 00:03:44.070
<b>Funada</b>

00:03:39.110 --> 00:03:40.570
Come at me in earnest, okay?

00:03:41.020 --> 00:03:43.480
I do have a black belt in kendo, 
believe it or not.

00:03:45.360 --> 00:03:47.020
Do you need any protective gear?

00:03:47.020 --> 00:03:49.030
I've never worn anything like that,

00:03:49.560 --> 00:03:50.840
so I'll stay as I am.

00:03:51.600 --> 00:03:53.680
I won't put any on either, then.

00:03:55.480 --> 00:03:56.570
Here we go!

00:03:59.370 --> 00:04:01.100
Refusing to cross your sword with mine...

00:04:01.810 --> 00:04:03.090
Don't underestimate me!

00:04:08.010 --> 00:04:09.430
Sorry.

00:04:10.130 --> 00:04:12.860
I don't clash swords when I fight.

00:04:13.680 --> 00:04:15.520
That only makes the blade dull.

00:04:20.440 --> 00:04:26.240
Though, that wouldn't be a concern 
if I had my treasured sword.

00:04:26.800 --> 00:04:28.240
Wow!

00:04:28.740 --> 00:04:30.080
This is great!

00:04:30.080 --> 00:04:33.330
You really are strong, Sensui!

00:04:34.790 --> 00:04:36.360
Kathleen-dono.

00:04:37.510 --> 00:04:39.100
I do have one more request!

00:04:39.100 --> 00:04:40.630
Stop using "dono" with me.

00:04:40.630 --> 00:04:42.080
Just Kathleen's fine.

00:04:44.500 --> 00:04:46.070
Oh, boy...

00:04:46.850 --> 00:04:47.880
Okay!

00:04:48.350 --> 00:04:49.480
That looks good on you!

00:04:51.540 --> 00:04:54.690
What's the point of this, Kathleen?

00:04:54.990 --> 00:04:57.730
There's no point. It's fashionable!

00:04:57.730 --> 00:04:58.540
Fashionable...?

00:04:59.190 --> 00:05:02.970
Times like these are all the more reason 
to dress up and boost your mood.

00:05:06.050 --> 00:05:07.950
What the hell?!

00:05:09.660 --> 00:05:11.030
What's the matter, Kenroku?!

00:05:12.570 --> 00:05:13.720
You...

00:05:16.280 --> 00:05:19.890
My head's turned blue!

00:05:21.920 --> 00:05:22.880
It looks great!

00:05:22.880 --> 00:05:25.380
It looks really good, 
just like I thought it would!

00:05:26.760 --> 00:05:29.720
This is what people are into now?

00:05:30.290 --> 00:05:34.960
Th-That's... quite vibrant.

00:05:37.680 --> 00:05:39.120
You're rocking it!

00:05:39.730 --> 00:05:42.720
A ninja with blue hair is totally cool!

00:05:42.720 --> 00:05:44.100
Don't you think so?

00:05:45.440 --> 00:05:47.240
Well, yeah.

00:05:48.350 --> 00:05:52.240
Now that I look closely, it's pretty sleek.

00:05:52.680 --> 00:05:53.950
Really?

00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:56.450
It is vibrant, but...

00:05:56.450 --> 00:05:59.930
It's bold and suits Kenroku so well, 
you'll know it's him from far away.

00:06:00.520 --> 00:06:04.000
Shinobi are finished 
if they stand out, though.

00:06:13.470 --> 00:06:15.350
Mom, sorry to keep you waiting!

00:06:15.870 --> 00:06:18.020
Oh, welcome home.

00:06:18.460 --> 00:06:21.770
Will you tell me stories 
about the Edo period?

00:06:27.440 --> 00:06:29.060
That'll do it.

00:06:29.060 --> 00:06:33.080
You're lucky you didn't get infected 
after being attacked by Gibia.

00:06:34.520 --> 00:06:38.310
Yurika-dono, if this is the future,

00:06:38.760 --> 00:06:42.170
do you know what happened 
in our era and afterward?

00:06:42.860 --> 00:06:46.260
Like what might have happened 
to Matsumoto Jouzen?

00:06:46.580 --> 00:06:48.220
Stop with the "dono".

00:06:48.220 --> 00:06:51.060
In this age, we use "san" for people.

00:06:52.430 --> 00:06:55.840
I do know a few things about 
what happened around the Edo era.

00:06:52.430 --> 00:06:58.930
<b>Warring States History - Records of Prominent Figures
Encyclopedia of Eastern Heroes
 Islands of Japan
Garden at the End of the World
The Mountain Folk</b>

00:06:56.660 --> 00:06:58.930
I happen to be a fan of period dramas.

00:06:59.970 --> 00:07:01.940
Yurika... san.

00:07:05.610 --> 00:07:07.440
If I recall correctly,

00:07:07.440 --> 00:07:10.950
that man kept betraying others 
until he was ultimately beheaded.

00:07:10.950 --> 00:07:12.650
Sensui!

00:07:12.650 --> 00:07:14.030
I beg of you!

00:07:14.030 --> 00:07:17.460
Tokugawa-dono won't demand too much from us!

00:07:17.450 --> 00:07:19.040
<b>Matsumoto Jouzen, Beheaded by Tokugawa</b>

00:07:17.450 --> 00:07:20.210
<b>The End of Tokugawa's 
Favored Warrior</b>

00:07:24.760 --> 00:07:27.990
<i>I can't believe it... My lord.</i>

00:07:34.470 --> 00:07:37.810
It's gotten late. I need to hurry!

00:08:05.490 --> 00:08:06.620
Maeda!

00:08:06.620 --> 00:08:09.000
Move quietly and don't panic!

00:08:24.390 --> 00:08:26.520
Aim the floodlights!

00:08:34.530 --> 00:08:37.030
Hurry, Maeda!

00:08:37.690 --> 00:08:40.040
I know, I know!

00:08:55.840 --> 00:08:59.960
He brought back a sword, 
but what good is that going to do?

00:09:00.570 --> 00:09:01.920
Who knows?

00:09:02.750 --> 00:09:06.160
If the Gibia start attacking, 
shine the lights on them immediately.

00:09:06.160 --> 00:09:07.020
Yes, sir.

00:09:16.790 --> 00:09:20.530
We can't be entertaining your mad whims.

00:09:20.530 --> 00:09:23.210
Adam. Sorry, man.

00:09:23.210 --> 00:09:25.540
I'll give you more shouchuu.

00:09:26.040 --> 00:09:28.540
I'll only accept the sweet potato kind.

00:09:29.200 --> 00:09:30.720
The buckwheat kind's good, too.

00:09:37.950 --> 00:09:40.320
Sensui, are you okay?

00:09:44.700 --> 00:09:49.790
Matsumoto Jouzen was 
the lord Sensui served.

00:09:49.860 --> 00:09:50.590
Huh?

00:09:50.590 --> 00:09:54.740
Apparently he felt obligated to him 
for taking him in as a child.

00:09:56.140 --> 00:09:57.380
I see.

00:10:00.180 --> 00:10:01.440
Sensui-kun.

00:10:06.080 --> 00:10:07.840
Yoshinaga-dono.

00:10:07.840 --> 00:10:11.250
Stop with the "dono," 
just Yoshinaga is fine.

00:10:12.150 --> 00:10:14.710
Are you done having your wound treated?

00:10:15.120 --> 00:10:17.760
Yeah, I'm done.

00:10:18.600 --> 00:10:20.130
What's the matter?

00:10:20.930 --> 00:10:22.260
Just a little thing.

00:10:35.280 --> 00:10:38.750
<i>My lord, what a regrettable end.</i>

00:10:39.540 --> 00:10:44.020
<i>What kind of retainer am I, if I couldn't be 
at your side in your final moments?!</i>

00:10:45.240 --> 00:10:49.250
<i>Was there any point to all my fighting?</i>

00:10:51.010 --> 00:10:54.260
<i>What was I even sent to a place like this for?</i>

00:10:55.670 --> 00:10:58.570
Oh, there you are! Samurai-san!

00:11:00.090 --> 00:11:01.770
Sorry for the wait!

00:11:02.110 --> 00:11:04.710
I brought my sword!

00:11:05.310 --> 00:11:06.730
Maeda-dono.

00:11:09.280 --> 00:11:10.110
This is bad!

00:11:10.110 --> 00:11:10.980
What's going on?

00:11:10.980 --> 00:11:11.780
The lights!

00:11:11.780 --> 00:11:12.750
The lights! Hurry up and turn them on!

00:11:12.750 --> 00:11:13.970
What? What's going on?!

00:11:13.970 --> 00:11:16.000
Gibia are attacking!

00:11:20.440 --> 00:11:21.870
Oh, no!

00:11:21.870 --> 00:11:23.490
Gibia are coming!

00:11:23.900 --> 00:11:26.650
Why?! What's going on?!

00:11:27.640 --> 00:11:29.630
The lights have gone out!

00:11:29.630 --> 00:11:32.510
At this rate, the Gibia will flood right in!

00:11:33.100 --> 00:11:36.750
Kathleen, you need to go to Yurika-san!

00:11:37.290 --> 00:11:40.410
Kenroku-kun, you come with me!

00:11:40.750 --> 00:11:43.750
We're going to intercept the Gibia 
with the defense team!

00:11:44.150 --> 00:11:45.260
Tch.

00:11:45.260 --> 00:11:47.810
Doctor! But what about Sensui?!

00:11:47.810 --> 00:11:49.220
Get going!

00:11:50.520 --> 00:11:51.390
Yes!

00:11:52.830 --> 00:11:53.810
Maeda-dono?!

00:12:07.690 --> 00:12:09.920
Take the sword!

00:12:15.590 --> 00:12:17.040
Maeda-dono!

00:12:22.470 --> 00:12:24.090
Maeda-dono!

00:12:36.530 --> 00:12:37.710
Maeda-dono!

00:13:07.760 --> 00:13:09.490
Samurai-san...

00:13:12.290 --> 00:13:13.580
Maeda-dono!

00:13:19.950 --> 00:13:22.010
Maeda-dono, are you all right?

00:13:23.200 --> 00:13:24.890
Just hold on a moment.

00:13:24.890 --> 00:13:29.460
Once I drive these enemies away, 
I'll take you to Kathleen's mother!

00:13:29.800 --> 00:13:32.490
It's fine, it's fine.

00:13:32.830 --> 00:13:36.300
Samurai-san, you really are strong.

00:13:38.480 --> 00:13:39.730
Hold on!

00:13:45.690 --> 00:13:47.760
You're so cool.

00:13:50.380 --> 00:13:52.090
Let my sword become lightning,

00:13:53.070 --> 00:13:56.730
to protect the common people!

00:13:58.310 --> 00:14:00.040
Come at me, Gibia!

00:14:05.970 --> 00:14:10.460
Hey, this is pretty bad, isn't it?

00:14:10.460 --> 00:14:13.610
Yeah, this is rather bad.

00:14:14.570 --> 00:14:16.670
With our lights out,

00:14:16.670 --> 00:14:20.500
this place is prime hunting grounds 
for Gibia that hate the light.

00:14:21.840 --> 00:14:24.500
Can't you fix them, Yoshinaga?

00:14:25.310 --> 00:14:29.430
Soon enough, even more Gibia 
will begin swarming around us.

00:14:29.820 --> 00:14:32.770
We have to come up with 
a plan before that happens.

00:14:33.780 --> 00:14:36.570
I don't know how effective this will be,

00:14:36.570 --> 00:14:39.350
but if we set the camp's 
tents on fire with torches

00:14:39.350 --> 00:14:41.900
we might be able to secure some light.

00:14:42.860 --> 00:14:44.910
Kenroku-kun, help me out.

00:14:46.550 --> 00:14:49.640
Maybe this really is the afterlife.

00:15:07.410 --> 00:15:08.300
Oh, my.

00:15:09.320 --> 00:15:11.920
Do you want to hear more about the Edo era?

00:15:16.560 --> 00:15:20.560
My, my, there's no need to rush like that.

00:15:27.660 --> 00:15:29.490
Mom, run!

00:15:37.930 --> 00:15:39.990
<i>Why did the lights go out?!</i>

00:15:39.990 --> 00:15:42.120
<i>We finally found some hope, too!</i>

00:15:48.010 --> 00:15:49.260
Damn it! Damn it!

00:16:01.800 --> 00:16:04.090
We'll never keep up like this!

00:16:04.450 --> 00:16:08.040
These flames aren't strong enough 
to frighten the Gibia!

00:16:11.950 --> 00:16:14.120
Shit, shit!

00:16:32.150 --> 00:16:35.230
Damn, it's heavy!

00:16:46.960 --> 00:16:48.290
Take that!

00:16:51.610 --> 00:16:53.840
Stay back! Stay back!

00:16:56.760 --> 00:17:00.870
Damn it! Quit attacking people,
 you bastards!

00:17:01.190 --> 00:17:03.870
Adam! They broke through the entrance!

00:17:03.870 --> 00:17:06.420
Fall back to the last line of defense!

00:17:06.930 --> 00:17:11.170
There aren't any damn lines when 
they're coming from all directions like this!

00:17:15.680 --> 00:17:16.680
Adam!

00:17:33.530 --> 00:17:35.510
I'll take over here!

00:17:35.870 --> 00:17:37.160
Take care of Kathleen!

00:17:37.850 --> 00:17:40.290
Shit, I'm not letting you—!

00:17:40.290 --> 00:17:41.390
Stop it, Adam!

00:17:42.560 --> 00:17:43.550
Sensui!

00:17:44.190 --> 00:17:46.540
Don't you go dying either!

00:18:14.530 --> 00:18:15.940
Oh, wow!

00:18:23.030 --> 00:18:25.470
That's the Slayer of a Thousand for you.

00:18:25.470 --> 00:18:28.040
Those Gibia are nothing before him.

00:18:43.870 --> 00:18:45.600
Kathleen, are you safe?!

00:18:45.600 --> 00:18:46.890
Adam!

00:18:47.890 --> 00:18:50.120
Sensui-kun came to save us!

00:18:50.120 --> 00:18:51.420
Come with us.

00:18:52.980 --> 00:18:54.730
Mom, let's go!

00:18:58.920 --> 00:19:00.170
Thank you.

00:19:00.170 --> 00:19:01.310
Hurry up and move!

00:19:01.310 --> 00:19:02.220
Yeah.

00:19:03.050 --> 00:19:04.390
Here they come, Adam!

00:19:20.760 --> 00:19:21.900
Sensui!

00:19:26.960 --> 00:19:27.990
Kenroku?!

00:19:30.220 --> 00:19:31.900
Let's keep on going!

00:19:51.980 --> 00:19:54.700
We have to make it through this,
 no matter what!

00:19:55.150 --> 00:19:57.840
We must protect the vaccine 
that will save this world!

00:19:59.900 --> 00:20:00.950
Doctor.

00:20:03.560 --> 00:20:04.760
Look at that!

00:20:14.010 --> 00:20:15.320
They're...

00:20:16.610 --> 00:20:18.040
that strong.

00:20:37.360 --> 00:20:41.610
Hey, man, he was still human. 
You didn't have to kill him.

00:20:41.990 --> 00:20:45.030
We were only able to 
kill him because of that.

00:20:45.370 --> 00:20:47.870
Once he turned into a Gibia, 
it wouldn't have been that simple.

00:20:49.240 --> 00:20:52.110
You're a quick learner, though, Kenroku-kun.

00:20:52.440 --> 00:20:55.310
You handled those grenades splendidly.

00:20:56.250 --> 00:20:59.620
I always had a thing for western stuff,

00:21:00.090 --> 00:21:03.320
so I'm pretty used to 
working with new things.

00:21:12.910 --> 00:21:14.330
Maeda-dono.

00:21:14.890 --> 00:21:18.830
Samurai-san, you won.

00:21:19.570 --> 00:21:20.590
Old man...

00:21:25.060 --> 00:21:28.590
Maeda-san, do you hear the sound of water?

00:21:29.820 --> 00:21:32.880
Yeah, I hear it.

00:21:33.210 --> 00:21:35.230
I've been hearing it for a while now.

00:21:36.440 --> 00:21:39.660
You've been infected 
with the Gibia Virus, then.

00:21:39.660 --> 00:21:40.860
No way!

00:21:42.560 --> 00:21:46.180
Samurai-san, you were so cool.

00:21:46.760 --> 00:21:49.370
I'm glad I got to see 
something great before the end.

00:21:53.370 --> 00:21:58.490
Ah, there's less and less 
time between the drips now.

00:22:00.160 --> 00:22:02.890
Please, Samurai-san.

00:22:07.510 --> 00:22:08.760
Maeda-dono!

00:22:12.220 --> 00:22:14.530
Before I become a Gibia!

00:22:25.200 --> 00:22:31.220
Farewell, Maeda-san.

00:22:45.800 --> 00:22:48.860
Kathleen-chan, Kathleen-chan!

00:22:48.860 --> 00:22:50.770
Huh? Maeda-san?

00:22:50.770 --> 00:22:52.990
Shh! Quiet!

00:22:52.990 --> 00:22:55.430
Yurika-san asked me to come here.

00:22:55.430 --> 00:22:57.070
Come with me!

00:22:57.070 --> 00:22:58.060
Come where?

00:22:58.060 --> 00:22:59.440
The back door!

00:23:00.170 --> 00:23:05.360
Gibia have entered the hospital, 
so those of us alive are running.

00:23:06.970 --> 00:23:08.440
Maeda-san!

00:23:09.440 --> 00:23:11.470
I'll protect you.

00:23:11.470 --> 00:23:13.670
You don't need to worry.

00:23:15.930 --> 00:23:17.200
Maeda-dono,

00:23:19.810 --> 00:23:21.260
thank you.

00:23:29.310 --> 00:23:33.840
I think it might be time to leave this area.

00:23:34.740 --> 00:23:37.590
There's not much food left here,

00:23:37.590 --> 00:23:40.640
so let's go somewhere else.

00:23:41.630 --> 00:23:45.630
Let's head out to a rural area next.

00:23:47.020 --> 00:23:51.230
We won't have trouble finding 
food in the countryside.

00:24:15.820 --> 00:24:16.720
Darling!

00:24:17.070 --> 00:24:18.450
Father!

00:24:22.890 --> 00:24:25.230
<b>"The Third Man"</b>
